{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_32812d565baeb9f4522742a5f580623b19eb86f465ad1e78367d6d7cd8a398f0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"sanbuphy/learn-coding-agent@ce8ca4a8e722 snapshot e96abc602fa9c456","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d9571949a5188a46e386147f4f6a8c0aebe0a993bf9ec79d854ea7195363785c"],"source_ids":["src_eb3f68c4732e52deacd2194c84bee553"],"text":"Context management uses three compression strategies: autoCompact (summarize old messages via an API call when tokens exceed a threshold), snipCompact, and contextCollapse, the latter two behind feature flags.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3c620221a7fe310d14dcc0ec56ecad6ea03e245e0ec20d47f30c70ff745b2ab9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"sanbuphy/learn-coding-agent@ce8ca4a8e722 snapshot e96abc602fa9c456","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0e0ce0def67cbe35870fb20c5131ea81fb3bdc06378919e543f54d107fc4f6b6","slc_ceea9852caf64b02e2dc066f2af70d0c32538c7f3d1ae0fd64b3c0bd65e8e57e"],"source_ids":["src_eb3f68c4732e52deacd2194c84bee553"],"text":"The documentation frames Claude Code as a minimal agent loop (call API, check stop_reason for tool_use, execute tools, append results) wrapped by a production harness adding permissions, streaming, concurrency, compaction, sub-agents, persistence, and MCP.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5035704f2989db7dbda9e93d5e91ca3f9a958918e1be301f46b0002cae5b557d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"sanbuphy/learn-coding-agent@ce8ca4a8e722 snapshot e96abc602fa9c456","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_82194024ec7fcb531fb6474fab05be57d1b4f84d57cdf56112c23223d9084911"],"source_ids":["src_eb3f68c4732e52deacd2194c84bee553"],"text":"The entry layer routes interactive use through a REPL and headless/SDK use through QueryEngine, whose submitMessage returns an AsyncGenerator of SDKMessages streamed to the consumer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_516b880a87f290c6a6159f98f743ffa4f4059fa8182bd1c3e99c7b41519e31a2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"sanbuphy/learn-coding-agent@ce8ca4a8e722 snapshot e96abc602fa9c456","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3f20d1c82a5f139364d1bf9f49f92db3162cbb752ba9d28367f693b958936098"],"source_ids":["src_eb3f68c4732e52deacd2194c84bee553"],"text":"The documented permission flow orders validateInput, user-defined PreToolUse hooks, always-allow/deny/ask rules from settings or CLI args, an interactive Allow Once/Always/Deny prompt, then tool-specific checkPermissions logic such as path sandboxing.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:19:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_36701d1b1617474ab7bf24222ca63999"}
